ober 2019)Google Scholar57YuT.QuillenD.HeZ.JulianR.HausmanK.FinnC.LevineS., (2020).Meta-world: a benchmark and evaluation for multi-task and Meta reinforcement learning.Available from:https://proceedings.mlr.press/v100/yu20a.html(Accessed 20 September 2024)Google Scholar58ZhanY.AmmarH. B.TaylorM. E.(2017).Scalable lifelong reinforcement learning.Pattern Recogn.72,407–418.Google Scholar59ZhangJ.WangJ.HuH.ChenT.ChenY.FanC.ZhangC.(2021).MetaCURE: Meta reinforcement learning with empowerment-driven exploration.Available from:https://proceedings.mlr.press/v139/zhang21w.html(Accessed 20 September 2024)Google ScholarSummaryKeywordsadvanced attack techniques,adversarial attacks,artificial intelligence,blackbox attacks,Carlini and Wagner attack (C&W),defense mechanisms,Fast Gradient Sign Method (FGSM),machine learningCitationRadanliev P, Santos O and Maple C (2026)Threats and vulnerabilities in artificial intelligence and agentic AI models.Front. Artif. Intell.9:1731566. doi:10.3389/frai.2026.1731566Received24 October 2025Revised26 December 2025Accepted07 January 2026Published13 February 2026Volume9 - 2026Edited byMohammad Akbari, Amirkabir University of Technology, IranReviewed byLiu Xinlei, Information Engineering University, ChinaKhedija Arour, Jeddah University, Saudi ArabiaUpdatesCheck for updatesCopyright© 2026 Radanliev, Santos and Maple.This is an open-access article distributed under the terms of theCreative Commons Attribution License (CC BY). The use, distribution or reproduction in other forums is permitted, provided the original author(s) and the copyright owner(s) are credited and that the original publication in this journal is cited, in accordance with accepted academic practice. No use, distribution or reproduction is permitted which does not comply with these terms.*Correspondence: Petar Radanliev,petar.radanliev@cs.ox.ac.uk†ORCID: Petar Radanliev,orcid.org/0000-0001-5629-6857DisclaimerAll claims expressed in this article are solely those of the authors and